      "body": "**Actionable comments posted: 13**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>src/utils.ts (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-25`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**월/년/CVC 검증의 배열 재생성을 줄여보는 게 좋겠습니다.**\n\n현재는 입력마다 `Array.from(...).map(...)`를 다시 만들어서 검사합니다. 상수 Set 사전계산 또는 숫자 범위 체크로 바꾸면 입력 중 검증 비용을 줄이고 코드 의도도 더 선명해집니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/utils.ts` around lines 13 - 25, The three validators (validateMonth,\nvalidateYear, validateCVC) recreate arrays on every call; refactor them to use\nprecomputed lookup Sets or simple numeric range checks instead: create\nmodule-level constants (e.g., MONTH_SET, YEAR_SET, CVC_SET) or replace\nincludes(...) with numeric comparisons (parseInt and range checks) and have\nvalidateMonth, validateYear, validateCVC reference those constants or ranges to\navoid rebuilding arrays each invocation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/components/CardForm.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`14-18`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**설명 텍스트는 heading보다 문단 태그가 더 적합합니다.**\n\n`Description`이 `h3`라서 문서 heading 구조를 불필요하게 늘립니다. 접근성/의미론 측면에서 `p` 사용을 권장합니다.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>제안 수정안</summary>\n\n```diff\n-const Description = styled.h3`\n+const Description = styled.p`\n   font-size: 10px;\n   color: var(--color-description);\n   margin: 0;\n `;\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardForm.tsx` around lines 14 - 18, The Description styled\ncomponent is declared as styled.h3 which adds an unnecessary heading; change the\ncomponent to a paragraph element by replacing styled.h3 with styled.p for the\nDescription component so the markup is semantic for descriptive text while\nkeeping the existing styles (font-size, color, margin) intact; update any\nimports or references if they rely on heading semantics.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/stories/CardExpiryDateInput.stories.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`45-47`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**`InvalidMonth` 스토리 이름과 실제 동작이 어긋나 있습니다.**\n\n현재 스토리는 초기값만 주입하고 있어 \"blur 후 에러 확인\" 상태를 자동 재현하지 않습니다. 이름을 조정하거나 `play`로 blur를 실제로 수행해 주세요.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/stories/CardExpiryDateInput.stories.tsx` around lines 45 - 47, The story\nInvalidMonth currently only sets initialMonth=\"13\" on the Wrapper but does not\nperform the user interaction implied by \"blur 후 에러 확인\"; update the story to\neither rename it to reflect a mere initial-value state or add a play function\nthat programmatically focuses and blurs the month input to trigger validation.\nLocate the InvalidMonth Story object and modify it: if adding interactions, use\nthe storybook play API to find the month input inside Wrapper (e.g., by\nrole/name or data-testid) and perform focus() then blur() so the component shows\nthe error; otherwise change the Story.name to something like \"Initial Invalid\nMonth\" to match current behavior. Ensure you reference the Wrapper component and\nthe InvalidMonth export when making the change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>src/stories/ValidationInput.stories.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`17-35`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**검증 스토리에서는 에러 메시지를 기본 노출하는 편이 상태 시각화에 유리합니다.**\n\n현재 Wrapper에서 `isShowError`를 넘기지 않아 검증 스토리의 피드백이 약합니다. `WithLimitValidation`/`WithCheckValidation`에서만 `isShowError`를 켜면 스토리 목적과 더 잘 맞습니다.  \n \n\n<details>\n<summary>수정 예시</summary>\n\n```diff\n function Wrapper({\n   initialValue,\n   validations,\n   placeholder,\n+  isShowError = false,\n }: {\n   initialValue: string;\n   validations: React.ComponentProps<typeof ValidationInput>['validations'];\n   placeholder?: string;\n+  isShowError?: boolean;\n }) {\n ...\n     <ValidationInput\n       value={value}\n       onChange={(e) => setValue(e.target.value)}\n       validations={validations}\n       placeholder={placeholder}\n+      isShowError={isShowError}\n     />\n   );\n }\n ...\n export const WithLimitValidation: Story = {\n   name: 'With Limit Validation (숫자만 허용)',\n   render: () => (\n     <Wrapper\n       initialValue=\"\"\n       placeholder=\"숫자만 입력\"\n+      isShowError={true}\n       validations={[\n ...\n export const WithCheckValidation: Story = {\n   name: 'With Check Validation (blur 시 검사)',\n   render: () => (\n     <Wrapper\n       initialValue=\"\"\n       placeholder=\"4자리 숫자\"\n+      isShowError={true}\n       validations={[\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 45-86\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/stories/ValidationInput.stories.tsx` around lines 17 - 35, The Wrapper\ncomponent used in the validation stories doesn't forward isShowError, so error\nmessages aren't visible; update Wrapper to accept an optional isShowError?:\nboolean prop and pass it through to the ValidationInput (i.e., add isShowError\nto the Wrapper props and include isShowError={isShowError} on the\n<ValidationInput>), then set isShowError={true} when rendering Wrapper in the\nWithLimitValidation and WithCheckValidation stories so those stories show\nvalidation errors by default.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@index.html`:\n- Line 2: The HTML root element currently uses lang=\"en\" which mismatches the\nKorean UI; update the <html> tag's lang attribute (the <html lang=\"en\">\noccurrence) to either \"ko\" or \"ko-KR\" to match the service language and improve\nscreen reader pronunciation and accessibility, then verify any localization/meta\ntags remain consistent with the change.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardExpiryDateInput.tsx`:\n- Line 97: In the CardExpiryDateInput component update the validation message\ntext to fix the typo: replace \"유효한 년도을 입력해주세요. (00 ~ 99)\" with the correct\nphrase \"유효한 연도를 입력해주세요. (00 ~ 99)\" inside the validation rule where the message\nis defined (search for the message string in CardExpiryDateInput).\n- Around line 20-25: CardExpiryDateInput currently initializes\nexpiryMonth/expiryYear from props.value and then maintains internal state,\ncausing desync when parent resets value; switch to a controlled pattern: stop\ntreating props.value as only initial state and either remove local state and\nread expiryMonth/expiryYear directly from props.value in render, calling\nprops.onChange([newMonth,newYear]) from your input handlers, or add a useEffect\nthat updates setExpiryMonth/setExpiryYear whenever props.value changes;\nupdate/keep references to expiryMonth, setExpiryMonth, expiryYear,\nsetExpiryYear, props.value, and props.onChange accordingly so parent-driven\nupdates always reflect in the UI.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardForm.tsx`:\n- Line 27: CardForm의 <form>이 기본 submit 동작을 허용해 Enter 입력 시 입력 상태가 유실되므로, CardForm\n컴포넌트의 form 요소에 onSubmit 핸들러를 추가해 이벤트의 기본 동작을 막아 주세요 (예: CardForm 내 form 태그에\nonSubmit={e => e.preventDefault()} 또는 별도 handleSubmit 함수에서 e.preventDefault()\n호출). 해당 수정은 form 태그와 CardForm 컴포넌트(또는 관련 handleSubmit 함수)를 수정하면 됩니다.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardNumberSegmentsInput.tsx`:\n- Around line 14-18: The component CardNumberSegmentsInput currently only\ninitializes segments from props.value and doesn't sync when props.value changes,\nbreaking the controlled contract; update the effect logic around segments and\nprops.onChange so that useEffect depends on [segments, props.value] and when\nprops.value changes call setSegments(props.value) (or alternatively remove local\nstate and read props.value directly to make it fully controlled); ensure you\navoid an infinite update loop by only calling setSegments(props.value) when\nprops.value !== segments (or use an appropriate equality check) and keep\nprops.onChange(segments) triggered only when segments actually change.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardPreview.tsx`:\n- Around line 43-44: The CardImage elements lack alt text which hurts\naccessibility; update both usages in CardPreview (the CardImage for chip.svg and\nthe conditional CardImage for props.cardBrand) to include alt attributes: for\npurely decorative chip.svg use alt=\"\" (empty string) and for the brand image use\na descriptive alt such as `${props.cardBrand} logo` or a localized equivalent,\nensuring the conditional still renders when props.cardBrand exists and that the\nalt derives from props.cardBrand.toLowerCase() only for the src while the alt\nuses the original brand name for clarity.\n\nIn `@src/components/Common/Flex.tsx`:\n- Around line 16-18: The conditional checks incorrectly tie flex-grow and\nflex-shrink to props.gap; update the styled component in Flex.tsx so each CSS\nproperty is emitted only when its own prop is provided: replace the gap-based\nconditions with checks against props.flexGrow and props.flexShrink (e.g.,\n(props) => (props.flexGrow != null ? `flex-grow: ${props.flexGrow};` : '') and\nsimilarly for flex-shrink) while keeping the existing gap line unchanged (use\nprops.gap for gap only) to avoid emitting undefined CSS.\n\nIn `@src/components/Common/InputErrorMessage.tsx`:\n- Line 7: In the InputErrorMessage component replace the fixed CSS rule \"height:\n14px;\" with a flexible layout: use \"min-height: 14px;\" and add wrapping rules\n(e.g., \"overflow-wrap: break-word;\" and \"white-space: pre-wrap;\") on the same\nstyled element (the styled error message element inside InputErrorMessage) so\nmulti-line error messages expand without overlapping following elements.\n\nIn `@src/components/Common/ValidationInput.tsx`:\n- Around line 69-70: In ValidationInput, the current line sets style={inputError\n? { borderColor: 'var(--color-error)' } : {}} which overwrites props.style;\nchange it to merge props.style with the error style so external styles are\npreserved (e.g., compute a mergedStyle from props.style and conditionally\napplied { borderColor: 'var(--color-error)' } based on inputError) and pass that\nmergedStyle to the element; locate this in the ValidationInput component where\nstyle is assigned and update usage of props.style and inputError accordingly.\n- Around line 50-56: The check-type validation (computed as failedValidation)\nincorrectly uses props.value, so blur validations don't run when the component\nis used with defaultValue/uncontrolled input; change the predicate to use the\ncurrent input value (the component's internal value state or the runtime value\npassed into the blur handler) instead of props.value so that\nvalidations.find(...) evaluates validation.validator(currentValue) for 'check'\nentries; update references to failedValidation and the validation.validator call\nto use that currentValue and ensure the length/existence check uses the runtime\nstring value.\n\nIn `@src/hooks/useCardBrand.ts`:\n- Around line 5-6: The MasterCard regex in useCardBrand.js incorrectly omits\nanchors for each alternative; update the test on CardNumberSegments[0] to use an\nanchored grouped pattern without the global flag, e.g. change\n/^(51)|(52)|(53)|(54)|(55)/g to /^(?:51|52|53|54|55)/ (or /^(51|52|53|54|55)$/\nif you need a full-string match) so each alternative is properly anchored to the\nstart and the global flag is removed.\n\nIn `@src/styles/index.css`:\n- Around line 1-2: The CSS uses `@import` with url(...) which violates the\nStylelint import-notation rule; replace the two `@import` url(...) statements (the\n`@import` for reset.css and the `@import` for the Pretendard CDN URL) with string\nnotation, i.e., use `@import` \"reset.css\"; and `@import`\n\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/.../pretendardvariable-dynamic-subset.min.css\"; to\nsatisfy the linter.\n\nIn `@src/utils.ts`:\n- Around line 1-3: validateNumberString currently treats a space as numeric\nbecause Number(' ') -> 0; update the character check to only accept digit\ncharacters. Replace the chars.every((char) => !isNaN(Number(char))) predicate\nwith a strict digit test such as /^[0-9]$/.test(char) (or char >= '0' && char <=\n'9') so only characters '0'–'9' pass (and ensure the function returns false for\nempty input if desired).\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@src/components/CardForm.tsx`:\n- Around line 14-18: The Description styled component is declared as styled.h3\nwhich adds an unnecessary heading; change the component to a paragraph element\nby replacing styled.h3 with styled.p for the Description component so the markup\nis semantic for descriptive text while keeping the existing styles (font-size,\ncolor, margin) intact; update any imports or references if they rely on heading\nsemantics.\n\nIn `@src/stories/CardExpiryDateInput.stories.tsx`:\n- Around line 45-47: The story InvalidMonth currently only sets\ninitialMonth=\"13\" on the Wrapper but does not perform the user interaction\nimplied by \"blur 후 에러 확인\"; update the story to either rename it to reflect a\nmere initial-value state or add a play function that programmatically focuses\nand blurs the month input to trigger validation. Locate the InvalidMonth Story\nobject and modify it: if adding interactions, use the storybook play API to find\nthe month input inside Wrapper (e.g., by role/name or data-testid) and perform\nfocus() then blur() so the component shows the error; otherwise change the\nStory.name to something like \"Initial Invalid Month\" to match current behavior.\nEnsure you reference the Wrapper component and the InvalidMonth export when\nmaking the change.\n\nIn `@src/stories/ValidationInput.stories.tsx`:\n- Around line 17-35: The Wrapper component used in the validation stories\ndoesn't forward isShowError, so error messages aren't visible; update Wrapper to\naccept an optional isShowError?: boolean prop and pass it through to the\nValidationInput (i.e., add isShowError to the Wrapper props and include\nisShowError={isShowError} on the <ValidationInput>), then set isShowError={true}\nwhen rendering Wrapper in the WithLimitValidation and WithCheckValidation\nstories so those stories show validation errors by default.\n\nIn `@src/utils.ts`:\n- Around line 13-25: The three validators (validateMonth, validateYear,\nvalidateCVC) recreate arrays on every call; refactor them to use precomputed\nlookup Sets or simple numeric range checks instead: create module-level\nconstants (e.g., MONTH_SET, YEAR_SET, CVC_SET) or replace includes(...) with\nnumeric comparisons (parseInt and range checks) and have validateMonth,\nvalidateYear, validateCVC reference those constants or ranges to avoid\nrebuilding arrays each invocation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪄 Autofix (Beta)</summary>\n\nFix all unresolved CodeRabbit comments on this PR:\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"4b0d0e0a-96d7-4f10-b296-3a18ea78f0b9\"} --> Push a commit to this branch (recommended)\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"ff5b1114-7d8c-49e6-8ac1-43f82af23a33\"} --> Create a new PR with the fixes\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: Organization UI\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n**Run ID**: `f6c80296-8975-487e-bba5-17c5d2388d4e`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 8d4c2c73f7cce87ffaae55245ae1cfd10228981d and 65a6fd5255543490ddaa2a81e211cd131b59be7f.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (6)</summary>\n\n* `package-lock.json` is excluded by `!**/package-lock.json`\n* `public/chip.svg` is excluded by `!**/*.svg`\n* `public/favicon.svg` is