{
  "path": "src/hooks/useCardBrand.ts",
  "line": 6,
  "body": "_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`In JavaScript regular expressions, what does /^(51)|(52)|(53)|(54)|(55)/ match, and why can it match values not starting with 5?`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nThe regex /^(51)|(52)|(53)|(54)|(55)/ matches strings that start with \"51\", \"52\", \"53\", \"54\", or \"55\". It does NOT match values not starting with 5. The premise that it can match such values is incorrect. Due to operator precedence in regex, | has the lowest precedence, so the pattern is parsed as (^51) | 52 | 53 | 54 | 55. The first alternative (^51) requires the string to start with \"51\". The other alternatives (52, etc.) are NOT anchored and can match anywhere, but since there is no $ anchor and it's likely used with .test or similar for full-string matching, those unanchored alternatives would only succeed if the *entire* string is exactly \"52\", etc., which still starts with 5. Examples: - \"51abc\" matches (^51) - \"52\" matches 52 alternative (full string) - \"a52\" does NOT match, because ^51 fails (doesn't start with 51), and 52 doesn't match the full \"a52\" - \"52abc\" matches 52 (partial match at start) To properly match strings starting with any of those, use /^(?:51|52|53|54|55)/.\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Regular_expressions/Disjunction\n- 2: https://www.regular-expressions.info/alternation.html\n- 3: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/32493884/regex-stops-after-match-and-does-not-match-further-when-using-alternation-symbol\n- 4: https://learnbyexample.github.io/learn_js_regexp/alternation-and-grouping.html\n- 5: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Operator_Precedence.\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**MasterCard 판별 정규식의 앵커링 문제를 수정하세요.**\n\n`Line 6`의 `/^(51)|(52)|(53)|(54)|(55)/g`는 연산자 우선순위로 인해 `(^51) | 52 | 53 | 54 | 55`로 파싱됩니다. 이는 `52`, `53`, `54`, `55` 대안들이 앵커되지 않아 문자열의 어디든 매칭될 수 있음을 의미합니다. 예를 들어 `\"5289\"`는 `52`에 의해 매칭되어 잘못 MasterCard로 판별될 수 있습니다.\n\n모든 대안에 앵커를 적용하려면 정규식을 `/^(?:51|52|53|54|55)$/` 또는 `/^(51|52|53|54|55)$/`로 변경해야 합니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/hooks/useCardBrand.ts` around lines 5 - 6, The MasterCard regex in\nuseCardBrand.js incorrectly omits anchors for each alternative; update the test\non CardNumberSegments[0] to use an anchored grouped pattern without the global\nflag, e.g. change /^(51)|(52)|(53)|(54)|(55)/g to /^(?:51|52|53|54|55)/ (or\n/^(51|52|53|54|55)$/ if you need a full-string match) so each alternative is\nproperly anchored to the start and the global flag is removed.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:hawk -->\n\n<!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->",
  "user": "coderabbitai[bot]",
  "html_url": "https://github.com/woowacourse/react-payments/pull/506#discussion_r3172578871"
